ere fully verified from API data vs inferred, what could NOT be checked (e.g. AccessDenied calls, IAM policy content you couldn't read, application code quality, cold-start behaviour, anything needing code inspection, other regions/accounts), possible false positives (e.g. a deprecated-runtime flag where the dates were or weren't verified in docs, functions intentionally low-memory), and the per-category confidence level (High/Medium/Low) with the reasoning. Do not overstate confidence; if any call failed or was throttled, say so."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Lambda functions in us-east-1 against best practices"}], "created_at": null}

